# Do not honour .gitignore / .git/info/exclude. A search rooted above a nested
# repository is otherwise silently empty whenever the outer repo ignores the
# inner one — and a blind result is indistinguishable from a clean one. What
# should never be searched is in ~/.ignore instead, which this does not disable.
--no-ignore-vcs

# Hidden directories hold the things most worth finding here — .agents,
# .claude, .github — and rg skips them by default. Git internals are the one
# thing --hidden would otherwise drag in, and VCS ignore is off above.
--hidden
--glob=!.git/

# A lowercase query matches any case; a query you deliberately capitalise stays
# exact. Same bargain as vim's smartcase, and it stops a search for a word that
# happens to be capitalised somewhere from coming back silently empty.
--smart-case
